nazuchem source and distribution provenance
==========================================

nazuchem was extracted from ReShiki, a molecular drawing application:
https://github.com/Ameyanagi/ReShiki
Original ReShiki/nazuchem contributions are Copyright (c) 2026 Ameyanagi
and ReShiki contributors, licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0. See LICENSE-MIT and
LICENSE-APACHE. Exception: original additions inside crates/nazuchem-n2s are
MIT only, like the OPSIN port they extend. Those terms do not replace
incorporated third-party terms.

Name to structure: nazuchem-n2s is a Rust port of OPSIN by Daniel Lowe,
Copyright 2017 Daniel Lowe, under MIT. The port began at OPSIN 2.9.0,
commit b91b610af5ab07560fedb20730d7aef46bb2bca0, and tracks upstream main
42e87ac6efb1bd9f578986f5ea7ee1faa8e93c91 (3.0-SNAPSHOT).
https://github.com/dan2097/opsin
Complete terms, source/resource pins and the port notice are in
crates/nazuchem-n2s/LICENSE, NOTICE, PORTING.md and provenance/.

Structure to name: nazuchem-s2n began as a port of openclatura 0.4.3,
commit 90dc5bcb4910c196122ec0405d06a32929a8f308, extended in ReShiki.
Copyright (c) 2026 lamalab-org; MIT.
https://github.com/lamalab-org/openclatura
It also incorporates OPSIN-derived registries and a CPython 3.12 integer-set
adaptation under Python-2.0. crates/nazuchem-s2n/NOTICE qualifies inherited
OPSIN generation pins and the unresolved CPython patch revision. Complete
terms, notices and CPython license history are in that crate's
licenses/openclatura/, licenses/opsin/ and licenses/cpython/.

Molecular perception: nazuchem-kernel adapts RDKit under BSD-3-Clause and
SiMolecule centres under BSD-2-Clause. crates/nazuchem-kernel/NOTICE records exact
revisions and incorporated scope. Complete terms and copyright notices are
in that crate's licenses/rdkit/ and licenses/centres/.
Shared naming vocabulary in nazuchem-ir is original ReShiki code under
MIT OR Apache-2.0; its NOTICE records the source history.

The facade's established package expression is:
(MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND MIT AND BSD-3-Clause AND BSD-2-Clause AND Python-2.0.
Each crate ships its applicable license texts and scope notice, and the
facade's licenses/ tree includes the complete engine/kernel terms. Copied
notices retain historical ReShiki paths and broader source inventories;
PROVENANCE-nazuchem.toml and the crate scope notices identify the subset
incorporated into this repository. Historical source pins remain unchanged.

Equal-key sorts use Rust's stable sort; no C++ standard library code is included.

crates/nazuchem-s2n/src/data/bluebook/p25_retained.tsv is retained as factual
data transcribed from IUPAC 2013 Recommendations P-25.2.1 Table 2.8.
It is excluded from the MIT/Apache-2.0 grant; its ledger licence remains
NOASSERTION (owner decision 2026-11-10).

tests/fixtures/s2n/bakeoff_corpus.tsv is a repository-only test fixture whose
CIDs and IUPAC names come from PubChem (NCBI). It is excluded from all published
crates, wheels and npm packages (owner decision 2026-11-10).
